title: Brest-Litovsk
face-image: img/events/brest.jpg
subtitle: The treaty, and the Left SRs.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 28 and bol_regime = 1 and at_war = 1
priority: 40
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.at_war = 0;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -20, army_discipline: 0, land_pressure: -5});
Q.lsr_left_gov = (Q.player_party == 'lsr') ? 0 : 1;
Q.fault_text = RO.fault(Q, 'brest');
!}

= Brest-Litovsk

On 3 March the Soviet government signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk with Germany and her allies: Russia lost Poland, the Baltic provinces, Ukraine and a quarter of her population, and a third of her industry. Lenin had to threaten to resign to get it ratified: Trotsky's formula, "neither war nor peace", had failed and the Germans had advanced on Petrograd.

Martov and Kamkov, the Left SR leader, both spoke against ratification. The Left SRs left the government on 19 March, over the treaty; the Soviet Congress ratified the treaty by 784 votes to 261. The war with Germany is over, for now.

[? if fault_flag = 1 : [+ fault_text +] ?]

- @against: Martov speaks against ratification.
- @joint: Propose a joint defence programme with the Left SRs.
- @accept: Accept the treaty as a necessity.
- @sr_against: Vote against ratification with the Left SRs.
- @sr_abstain: Abstain, and say that the peasants have not been asked.
- @lsr_leave: Leave the government over the treaty.
- @lsr_stay: Stay in the government and fight the treaty from inside.
- @lsr_vote: Vote for ratification.
- @lsr_front: Form an anti-Brest front with the Mensheviks.

@against
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik'
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 6, rel_bol: -2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 5);
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 1, middle: 1});
!}

Martov spoke for the opposition: "the treaty is a shame, but your signing it is a disaster". It was the best speech of the Congress, and it was heard by nobody who mattered.

@joint
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik'
choose-if: rel_lsr >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: The Left SRs will not talk to us.
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 12, rel_bol: -3});
if (Q.ally_lsr < 1) { Q.ally_lsr = 1; }
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 5);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, 3);
Q.anti_brest_front = 1;
!}

An anti-Brest front of Mensheviks and Left SRs has been formed, on paper. It has a common programme for a revolutionary defence: a people's militia, not a standing army, and a refusal to ratify.

@accept
view-if: player_party != 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 3, rel_lsr: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

We accepted the treaty as a fact. The Left SRs called it a betrayal of the revolution, and left the government.

@sr_against
view-if: player_party = 'sr'
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 6, rel_bol: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 1, middle: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 2, -4);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
!}

The SR delegates voted with the Left SRs against the treaty. It is a shameful peace; nobody in the party disagrees about that. The question is what the party proposes in its place, and the answer is a revolutionary war that nobody has the soldiers for.

@sr_abstain
view-if: player_party = 'sr'
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 2);
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 1});
!}

We abstained, and said that a peace which the peasants and soldiers have not been asked about is the Assembly's business. The Left SRs called it cowardice.

@lsr_leave
view-if: player_party = 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_in_gov = 0;
Q.lsr_seats = 0;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -10, soviet_democracy: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3, peasants: 3, middle: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 12);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, -2);
Q.anti_brest = (Q.anti_brest || 0) + 1;
!}

On 19 March the Left SR People's Commissars resigned from the government, over the Treaty and over what they say is the abandonment of the revolutionary war. The seven commissariats were given to Bolsheviks within a week. The party is a party of opposition again, with a seat on the Cheka's board and a reputation for courage.

@lsr_stay
view-if: player_party = 'lsr' and lsr_in_gov = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.brest_rb = Q.rel_bol; Q.brest_sd = Q.soviet_democracy;
Q.stay_p = RO.clamp((Q.rel_bol - 60) / 50 + (Q.soviet_democracy - 50) / 200 + 0.05 * Q.bloc_lean + 0.08 * Q.anti_brest_front, 0.05, 0.9);
Q.stay_ok = (Q.dissent < 0.45 && RO.chance(Q.stay_p)) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.stay_ok) {
    Q.seven_commissars = 1;
    RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 3, soviet_democracy: 1});
    RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, peasants: 2});
    RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
} else {
    Q.lsr_in_gov = 0;
    Q.lsr_seats = 0;
    RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -6, soviet_democracy: -2});
    RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 1, peasants: 1});
    RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 8);
}
!}
go-to: lsr_stay_yes if stay_ok = 1; lsr_stay_no if stay_ok = 0

@lsr_stay_yes

The Left SR commissars voted against the treaty in the Council of People's Commissars and in the Congress of Soviets, and stayed at their posts. Lenin, who needs the peasants' party more than he cares to say, allowed it. The first coalition in Russian history has survived a vote on a matter of principle.

@lsr_stay_no

The Left SR commissars voted against the treaty and said that they were staying. Lenin told them that a government that voted in two ways was not a government, and that they would be treated as an opposition. The Left SR commissariats were reorganised in the course of the week.

@lsr_vote
view-if: player_party = 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 6});
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -3, soldiers: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -3, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 8);
if (Q.lsr_in_gov) { Q.seven_commissars = 1; }
!}

The party voted for ratification, with a heavy heart, and stayed in the government. The village delegations say that the Left SRs have become the Bolsheviks' junior partner. In the Baltic Fleet, they say worse.

@lsr_front
view-if: player_party = 'lsr'
choose-if: rel_lsr >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: The Mensheviks will not stand beside us.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ally_lsr < 1) { Q.ally_lsr = 1; }
Q.anti_brest_front = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_lsr: 10, rel_bol: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, peasants: 1, middle: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 1, 2);
Q.anti_brest = (Q.anti_brest || 0) + 1;
!}

Martov and Kamkov spoke against ratification from the same platform. The Menshevik Internationalists and the Left SRs have published a joint declaration: no ratification without a vote of the Constituent Assembly, no peace over the heads of the German workers. It is the only front in the Congress that includes both parties.
